### identity-service — direct API calls. Mints JWTs + publishes JWKS.

@identity = http://localhost:5300
@sellerId = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@buyerId  = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@adminId  = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333

### Mint a Seller token
GET {{identity}}/demo/token?role=Seller&userId={{sellerId}}

### Mint a Buyer token
GET {{identity}}/demo/token?role=Buyer&userId={{buyerId}}

### Mint an Admin token
GET {{identity}}/demo/token?role=Admin&userId={{adminId}}

### OIDC discovery — what relying parties (BFFs + services) read on startup
GET {{identity}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

### JWKS — public key for token validation. JwtBearer middleware in services + BFFs
### fetches this and caches the result.
GET {{identity}}/.well-known/jwks.json

### Health probe (used by docker-compose health checks + CI wait loop)
GET {{identity}}/health
